{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Backtest | ISDS Thematic Watcher{% endblock %}
{% block description %}A small exploratory backtest of the deterministic scorer on a focused set of known investor&ndash;State cases &mdash; the three seed awards, four out-of-sample positives, and clear off-theme negatives &mdash; with a confusion matrix and a per-case breakdown.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="measure">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="{{ root }}index.html">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Backtest</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <p class="page-kicker">Scorer evaluation</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Historical backtest</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      A small exploratory backtest on known cases &mdash; not a comprehensive validation.
      It scores {{ bt.total }} familiar investor&ndash;State cases with the same deterministic
      keyword scorer the pipeline uses, at the same digest threshold ({{ bt.threshold }}), and
      reports where it agrees with the label and where it misses.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="measure">
    <h2 class="section-head">What this is, and is not</h2>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <p>
        This page is an honest, narrow sanity check, not a validation study. The set is
        only {{ bt.total }} cases, hand-picked because they are well known, and it deliberately
        mixes two kinds of case:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          the three <strong>development seed awards</strong> (Eli&nbsp;Lilly v.&nbsp;Canada,
          Philip&nbsp;Morris v.&nbsp;Australia, Bridgestone v.&nbsp;Panama). These are
          <em>in-sample</em> &mdash; their vocabulary trained the fingerprint &mdash; so passing
          them confirms the scorer recovers what it was built on, nothing more;
        </li>
        <li>
          four <strong>out-of-sample positives</strong> (Loewen, Mondev, Apotex, Philip&nbsp;Morris
          v.&nbsp;Uruguay) and clear <strong>off-theme negatives</strong>, drawn from the labelled
          holdout. These were not used in development, so they test generalisation.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Every case&rsquo;s text comes from material already in the repository &mdash; the seeds from
        their verbatim seed-tagged phrases in <code>fingerprint.yaml</code>, the holdout items
        verbatim from <code>holdout_set.json</code>. Nothing here is fabricated, and any case whose
        text could not be resolved in-repo was excluded rather than invented. Read it as a smoke
        test with a candid record of its one miss, not as evidence of field performance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-alt">
  <div class="measure">
    <h2 class="section-head">Confusion matrix</h2>
    <p class="page-lede" style="font-size:16.5px; margin:0 0 22px;">
      Predicted band at or above the threshold counts as a predicted match; below it counts as a
      predicted pass. Rows are the true label; columns are the prediction.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">
          Confusion matrix of predicted match versus true label across {{ bt.total }} cases.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted match (&#8805;&nbsp;{{ bt.threshold }})</th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted pass (&lt;&nbsp;{{ bt.threshold }})</th>
            <th scope="col">Row total</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">On-theme (label&nbsp;=&nbsp;1)</th>
            <td><strong>TP {{ bt.tp }}</strong></td>
            <td>FN {{ bt.fn }}</td>
            <td>{{ bt.n_pos }}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Off-theme (label&nbsp;=&nbsp;0)</th>
            <td>FP {{ bt.fp }}</td>
            <td><strong>TN {{ bt.tn }}</strong></td>
            <td>{{ bt.n_neg }}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Headline metrics derived from the confusion matrix.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Precision</th>
            <th scope="col">Recall</th>
            <th scope="col">Accuracy</th>
            <th scope="col">F1</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>{{ '%.2f' | format(bt.precision) }}</td>
            <td>{{ '%.2f' | format(bt.recall) }}</td>
            <td>{{ '%.2f' | format(bt.accuracy) }}</td>
            <td>{{ '%.2f' | format(bt.f1) }}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        On this focused set the scorer makes
        {{ bt.fp + bt.fn }} miss{{ 'es' if (bt.fp + bt.fn) != 1 else '' }}:
        {{ bt.fn }} false negative{{ 's' if bt.fn != 1 else '' }} and
        {{ bt.fp }} false positive{{ 's' if bt.fp != 1 else '' }}. The misses are listed in full
        below &mdash; the point of a backtest is the failures, not the passes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="measure">
    <h2 class="section-head">Per-case results</h2>
    <p class="page-lede" style="font-size:16.5px; margin:0 0 22px;">
      Every case, its label, the score the deterministic scorer assigned, the predicted band, and
      a note on any miss. Positives (seeds, then out-of-sample) first, then negatives.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">
          Per-case backtest results: case, group, label, score, predicted band, and miss note.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Case</th>
            <th scope="col">Group</th>
            <th scope="col">Label</th>
            <th scope="col">Score</th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted band</th>
            <th scope="col">Note</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in bt.cases %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ c.name }}</th>
            <td>{{ c.group }}</td>
            <td>{{ 'on-theme' if c.label == 1 else 'off-theme' }}</td>
            <td>{{ c.score }}</td>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-{{ c.band | band_class }}">{{ c.band }}</span>
            </td>
            <td>
              {% if c.correct %}correct{% else %}<strong>{{ c.miss_kind }}</strong>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if bt.false_negatives or bt.false_positives %}
<section class="band band-alt">
  <div class="measure">
    <h2 class="section-head">Where it misses, and why</h2>
    <div class="doc-body">
      {% if bt.false_negatives %}
      <h3>False negatives</h3>
      <ul>
        {% for c in bt.false_negatives %}
        <li><strong>{{ c.name }}</strong> (score {{ c.score }}). {{ c.reason }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
      {% if bt.false_positives %}
      <h3>False positives</h3>
      <ul>
        {% for c in bt.false_positives %}
        <li><strong>{{ c.name }}</strong> (score {{ c.score }}). {{ c.reason }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="archive-foot">
      See the <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html">methodology</a> for how the scorer and its
      threshold are defined.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
